1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,360
A million dollars loses to a hundred bucks a day.

2
00:00:03,900 --> 00:00:07,320
Wait, how? Picture two piles of money on a table.

3
00:00:07,820 --> 00:00:10,360
On the left, one million dollars cash, today.

4
00:00:10,900 --> 00:00:14,360
On the right, a hundred dollars every day, for the rest of your life.

5
00:00:14,880 --> 00:00:17,320
No taxes, no interest, just the money.

6
00:00:17,840 --> 00:00:19,860
Tap the heart if your hand already went for the million.

7
00:00:20,380 --> 00:00:24,580
Now let's race them. Every morning, another hundred dollar bill lands on the pile.

8
00:00:25,020 --> 00:00:28,220
That's about three thousand a month, basically your rent, forever.

9
00:00:28,680 --> 00:00:30,180
Year one, the pile hits thirty-six thousand five hundred dollars.

10
00:00:32,560 --> 00:00:36,780
Year ten? Three hundred sixty-five thousand. Still way behind.

11
00:00:37,380 --> 00:00:41,020
Then on day ten thousand, the little pile finally catches the million.

12
00:00:41,440 --> 00:00:43,080
That's about twenty-seven years in.

13
00:00:43,620 --> 00:00:45,920
Send this to the friend who says, just give me the million.

14
00:00:46,380 --> 00:00:49,400
But here's the catch. The pile only grows while you're alive.

15
00:00:50,020 --> 00:00:53,560
Start at twenty-five, live to eighty, and you end up with about two million.

16
00:00:54,020 --> 00:00:56,000
Follow if you just checked how old you are.

17
00:00:56,000 --> 00:00:59,040
But start at sixty and live to eighty, and you only get seven hundred thirty thousand.

18
00:01:01,040 --> 00:01:02,120
The million wins by two hundred seventy thousand dollars.

19
00:01:04,760 --> 00:01:08,320
So it was never about the money. It's how many years you've got left.

20
00:01:08,820 --> 00:01:11,120
Million or a hundred a day? One word.

